dialogue cohesion_barbarian_redmage
title: Two fires
trigger: Cohesion barbarian redmage level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker barbarian barbarian
speaker redmage redmage

node open commander
  The Red Mage sits on the upturned crate with the dented tin open. The Barbarian has dragged a log over to the same patch of dark and is watching the coal as if it might bite.
  -> ask

node ask barbarian
  Every night, that tin. I've watched it since the fen. Let me hold it.
  -> no

node no redmage
  No. Nobody holds it. It came out of my aunt's hearth the morning of her tithe, and it's been in my hands or my coat for nine years. That's the arrangement.
  -> grey

node grey barbarian
  Tithe. Aye. Mine was my brother. Came home grey and sat by a door all winter. You carry a fire that won't go out. I carry one I'd put out tomorrow if I knew how.
  -> fool

node fool redmage
  And I'd walk into the sea before I let mine go out. So which of us is the fool, Commander? The one who keeps it burning, or the one who wants it gone?
  * Neither. You both kept something the Choir couldn't take. -> kept
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:fire_kept
  * Let the Barbarian hold the tin, just for tonight. -> hold
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage 10
    do: AddTrust redmage -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:fire_held
  * The Barbarian's right. A fire with no use is a risk to the wagons. -> risk
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage -4
    do: AddTrust redmage -2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:fire_risk
  * I said the coal was what the tithe couldn't take. The red is the same thing, burning the other way. -> honoured
    if: FlagSet redmage:coal_honoured
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage 8
    do: AddTrust redmage 2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:fire_honoured

node kept redmage
  Kept. Hm. I've never thought of a temper as a keepsake. You'd be a very bad tin, Barbarian.
  -> brother

node hold redmage
  Tonight. Fine. Two hands, and level, and if you sneeze I'll set your eyebrows alight. There. It's lighter than you thought, isn't it?
  -> brother

node risk redmage
  A risk. Everything worth carrying is. I'll keep the lid lower, Commander, the way I always do when someone tells me that.
  -> brother

node honoured redmage
  Burning the other way. Outward instead of in. That's exactly it. My hands got the burns. Yours went out to a collector's arm.
  -> brother

node brother barbarian
  That orb of the Commander's wakes up near dead things. You've been eyeing it. If fire near the Commander can reach a Hollow, could it reach a grey one? Could it reach him?
  * We said we'd try on a Hollow, together. Saltmoss is where we try first. -> saltmoss
    if: FlagSet redmage:test_promised
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage 10
    do: AddTrust barbarian 3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:try_saltmoss
  * Teach the Barbarian to bank the coal. Two keepers are better than one. -> keepers
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage 8
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:try_keepers
  * No promises tonight. Neither of you burns yourself for a guess. -> guess
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage 4
    do: AddTrust redmage -2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:try_guess
  * Your brother's still alive in Saltmoss. That's a road, and we'll walk it. -> road
    if: FlagSet barbarian:tithe_home
    do: AddCohesion barbarian redmage 6
    do: AddTrust barbarian 2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_redmage:try_road

node saltmoss redmage
  Saltmoss first. Then my aunt's kitchen. I'll hold the coal, you hold the door, and the Commander does whatever it is the Commander does. That's a plan, Barbarian. I like a plan.
  -> close

node keepers barbarian
  Me? I'd smother it. Show me anyway. Peat and a breath, aye? Slow. Slower than that. I'm not good at slow.
  -> close

node guess barbarian
  Guesses are all I've had for years. Fine. No burning. But I'm asking again, Commander, when there's more than a guess.
  -> close

node road redmage
  A road. Then I'll carry the coal along it. A cold house is a cold house, wherever it is. Mine or yours.
  -> close

node close commander
  The lid clicks half shut. For a while two faces sit in the small red glow through the dent, saying nothing, and neither one moves to leave.
